From 8f3a69f6407e773489480adc8f74b5de3c9c3d64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mod Loader Android port <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:38:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Android port: do not refuse already-hooked functions, handle
 Android_unprotected, better diagnostics

Found on a real device (modloader.log): "OS_FileOpen does not look like the one of
GTA SA 2.00, refusing to hook it" - the plugins never started and the scanned mod was
not applied. The libGTASA.so in use loads the Fastman92 plugin loader, which hooks
functions at run time, so the first bytes of the function are a jump, not the original
prologue.

* Hook-target check now has three outcomes: the analysed code, code that starts like an
  inline hook (ldr.w pc,[pc] / b.w / bx pc / ARM ldr pc,[pc,#-4]) which is accepted and
  hooked on top of, and anything else, which is a warning (found/expected bytes are
  logged) unless StrictChecks = true in config.ini.
* MakeGameName looked for "/Android/" but NvFOpen uses strstr(root, "/Android"): the game
  folder of that device is ".../Android_unprotected/data/...". Same rule as the game now.
* The log starts with the path/size/FNV-1a hash of the libGTASA.so that is really running.
* std.stream notices when the streaming info array it knows is not the one the game
  fills (moved by a limit adjuster) and disables IMG patching instead of writing into it.
* FNV offset basis fixed to the standard constant.
* Tests: 249 checks (hook target classification, storage paths, relocated infos, strict
  and non-strict startup).
